/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Everything the harness produces. Generated C, run records, reports and the scratch
# directory the compilers write objects into. All of it is regenerable from a commit hash
# and a toolchain list, which is the point.
/out
/generated
*.profraw
*.profdata

# Everything a run generates that is not markdown. The raw record of every build, the JSON
# summary the tools read, the SARIF the code scanning upload reads, and the machine readable
# copy of the program list. All four are regenerated on every night whether or not anything
# about the compiler moved, so committing them makes the history churn and makes the diff
# something nobody reads. What gets committed is the markdown, which is a page a person opens
# and a diff a person can follow. CI uploads all of these as build artifacts, so when a number
# in a report needs chasing back to the build that produced it, the record is there.
/reports/runs.jsonl
/reports/report.json
/reports/findings.sarif
/programs/manifest.json

.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
